{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2.5 d stereo motion graphics 2.5 d stereo motion graphics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","fileName":"2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Stereoscopic Imaging and Conversion]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Stereoscopic Imaging and Conversion","2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"2.5 d stereo motion graphics 2.5 d stereo motion graphics","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","fileName":"2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics","heading":"2.5D Stereo Motion Graphics","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Flat artwork can still contribute to a stereo sequence when separate cards are arranged at different depths. The book stages parchment, silhouettes, and text cards in a 3D scene, animates them, and records the result with offset left and right virtual cameras. The images themselves remain two-dimensional, but the cards' placement gives them binocular parallax. The method works especially well for titles and stylized artwork that do not require a camera orbit around volumetric forms. See [[2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Stereoscopic Imaging and Conversion","2.5D Depth Cards and Parallax","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"prope